G1715.b:
⟪ἔμ-προσθεν⟫ adv. of place (in cl. also of time),
[in LXX chiefly for ⁨עֳנִי⁩ ;]
⟪1.⟫ adverbially, ⟪before, in front⟫: ⟦Luke 19:28|Lk 19:28⟧; εἰς τὸ ἔ., ⟦Luke 19:4|Lk 19:4⟧; opp. to ὄπισθεν, ⟦Revelation 4:6|Re 4:6⟧; opp. to τὰ ὀπίσω, τὰ ἔ., ⟦Philippians 3:13|Phl 3:13⟧.
⟪2.⟫ As prep., ⟪before⟫;
⟪(a)⟫ in front of: ⟦Matthew 5:24|Mt 5:24⟧ ⟦Matthew 6:2|6:2⟧ ⟦Matthew 7:6|7:6⟧ ⟦Matthew 11:10|11:10⟧ ⟦Matthew 27:29|27:29⟧, ⟦Luke 5:19|Lk 5:19⟧ ⟦Luke 7:27|7:27⟧ ⟦Luke 14:2|14:2⟧, ⟦John 3:28|Jo 3:28⟧ ⟦John 10:4|10:4⟧, ⟦Revelation 19:10|Re 19:10⟧ ⟦Revelation 22:8|22:8⟧;
⟪(b)⟫ in the presence of: ⟦Matthew 27:11|Mt 27:11⟧, ⟦Galatians 2:14|Ga 2:14⟧, ⟦1 Thessalonians 1:3|I Th 1:3⟧ ⟦1 Thessalonians 2:19|2:19⟧ ⟦1 Thessalonians 3:9|3:9⟧ ⟦1 Thessalonians 3:13|3:13⟧; ὁμολουεῖν, ἀρνεῖσθαι (Dalman, Words, 210), ⟦Matthew 10:32|Mt 10:32⟧, ⟦Matthew 10:33|33⟧ ⟦Matthew 26:70|26:70⟧, ⟦Luke 12:8|Lk 12:8⟧; in forensic sense, ⟦Matthew 25:32|Mt 25:32⟧ ⟦Matthew 27:11|27:11⟧, ⟦Luke 21:36|Lk 21:36⟧, ⟦Acts 18:17|Ac 18:17⟧, ⟦2 Corinthians 5:10|II Co 5:10⟧, ⟦1 Thessalonians 2:19|I Th 2:19⟧, ⟦1 John 3:19|I Jn 3:19⟧; εὐδοκία (θέλημά) ἐστι ἔ. θεοῦ (a targumic formula; Dalman, Words, 211), ⟦Matthew 11:26|Mt 11:26⟧ ⟦Matthew 18:14|18:14⟧, ⟦Luke 10:21|Lk 10:21⟧;
⟪(c)⟫ in the sight of: ⟦Matthew 5:16|Mt 5:16⟧ ⟦Matthew 6:1|6:1⟧ ⟦Matthew 17:2|17:2⟧ ⟦Matthew 23:14|23:14⟧, ⟦Mark 2:12|Mk 2:12⟧ ⟦Mark 9:2|9:2⟧, ⟦Luke 19:27|Lk 19:27⟧, ⟦John 12:37|Jo 12:37⟧, ⟦Acts 10:4|Ac 10:4⟧;
⟪(d)⟫ of rank and dignity (Dem., Plat., al.; LXX, ⟦Genesis 48:20|Ge 48:20⟧): ⟦John 1:15|Jo 1:15⟧, ⟦John 1:30|30⟧.†

G1722.b:
⟪ἐν⟫, prep, (the most freq. of all in NT), c. dat. (= Heb. ⁨בְּ⁩, Lat. in, c. abl.).
⟪I.⟫ Of place, c. dat. rei, pers., ⟪in, within, on, at, by, among⟫: ἐν τ. πόλει, ⟦Luke 7:37|Lk 7:37⟧; τ. οφθαλμῷ, ⟦Matthew 7:3|Mt 7:3⟧; τ. κοιλίᾳ, ⟦Matthew 12:40|Mt 12:40⟧; τ. ὄρει, ⟦2 Peter 1:18|II Pe 1:18⟧; τ. θρόνῳ, ⟦Revelation 3:21|Re 3:21⟧; τ. δεξιᾷ τ. θεοῦ, ⟦Romans 8:34|Ro 8:34⟧; ἐν ἡμῖν Abbott-Smith has ὑμῖν., ⟦Luke 1:1|Lk 1:1⟧; of books, ἐν τ. βιβλίῳ, ⟦Galatians 3:10|Ga 3:10⟧; τ. νόμῳ, ⟦Matthew 12:5|Mt 12:5⟧, al.; ἐν τοῖς τ. Πατρός, ⟪in my Father's house⟫ (RV; cf. M, Pr., 103), ⟦Luke 2:49|Lk 2:49⟧; trop., of the region of thought or feeling, ἐν τ. καρδίᾳ (-αις), ⟦Matthew 5:28|Mt 5:28⟧, ⟦2 Corinthians 4:6|II Co 4:6⟧, al.; τ. συνειδήσεσιν, ⟦2 Corinthians 5:11|II Co 5:11⟧; after verbs of motion, instead of εἰς (constructio praegnans, a usage extended in late Gk. beyond the limits observed in cl.; cf. Bl., §41, 1; M, Th., 12), ἀποστέλλω . . . ἐν, ⟦Matthew 10:16|Mt 10:16⟧. δέδωκεν ἐν τ. χειρί (cf. τιθέναι ἐν χερσί, Hom., Il., i, 441, al.), ⟦John 3:35|Jo 3:35⟧; id. after verbs of coming and going (not in cl.), εἰσῆλθε, ⟦Luke 9:46|Lk 9:46⟧; ἐξῆλθεν, ⟦Luke 7:17|Lk 7:17⟧.
⟪II.⟫ Of state, condition, form, occupation, etc.: ἐν ζωῇ, ⟦Romans 5:10|Ro 5:10⟧; ἐν τ. θανάτῳ, ⟦1 John 3:14|I Jo 3:14⟧; ἐν πειρασμοῖς, ⟦1 Peter 1:6|I Pe 1:6⟧; ἐν εἰρήνῃ, ⟦Mark 5:25|Mk 5:25⟧; ἐν δόξῃ, ⟦Philippians 4:19|Phl 4:19⟧; ἐν πραΰτητι, ⟦James 3:13|Ja 3:13⟧; ἐν μυστηρίῳ, ⟦1 Corinthians 2:7|I Co 2:7⟧; ἐν τ. διδαχῇ, ⟦Mark 4:2|Mk 4:2⟧; of a part as contained in a whole, ἐν τ. ἀμπέλῳ, ⟦John 15:4|Jo 15:4⟧; ἐν ἑνὶ σώματι, ⟦Romans 12:4|Ro 12:4⟧; of accompanying objects or persons (simple dat. in cl.), ⟪with⟫, ἐν αἵματι, ⟦Hebrews 9:25|He 9:25⟧; ἐν δέκα χιλιάσιν, ⟦Luke 14:31|Lk 14:31⟧ (cf. ⟦Jude 1:14|Ju 14⟧, ⟦Acts 7:14|Ac 7:14⟧); similarly (cl.), of clothing, armour, arms, ἐν στολαῖς, ⟦Mark 12:38|Mk 12:38⟧; ἐν ἐσθῆτι λαμπρᾷ, ⟦James 2:2|Ja 2:2⟧; ἐν μαξαίρῃ, ⟦Luke 22:49|Lk 22:49⟧; ἐν ῥάβδῳ, ⟦1 Corinthians 4:21|I Co 4:21⟧ (cf. ἐν τόξοις, Xen., Mem., 3, 9, 2); of manner (cl.), ἐν τάχει (= ταχέως), ⟦Luke 18:8|Lk 18:8⟧ (cf. Bl., §41, 1); of spiritual influence, ἐν πνεύματι, ⟦Romans 8:9|Ro 8:9⟧; ἐν π. ἀκαθάρτῳ, ⟦Mark 1:23|Mk 1:23⟧; of the mystical relation of the Christian life and the believer himself, to God and Christ (cf. ICC, Ro., 160f.; Mayor on ⟦Jude 1:1|Ju 1⟧; M, Pr., 103): ἐν Χριστῷ, ⟦Romans 3:24|Ro 3:24⟧, ⟦Romans 6:11|6:11⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 3:1|I Co 3:1⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 4:10|4:10⟧, ⟦2 Corinthians 12:2|II Co 12:2⟧, ⟦Galatians 2:17|Ga 2:17⟧, ⟦Ephesians 6:21|Eph 6:21⟧, ⟦Colossians 4:7|Col 4:7⟧, ⟦1 Thessalonians 4:16|I Th 4:16⟧, al.
⟪III.⟫ Of the agent, instrument or means (an extension of cl. ἐν of instr.—v. LS, s.v. Ill—corresponding to similar use of Heb. ⁨בְּ⁩), ⟪by, with⟫: ἐν ὑμῖν κρίνεται ὁ κόσμος (= cl. παρά, C. dat.), ⟦1 Corinthians 6:2|I Co 6:2⟧; ἐν τ. ἄρχοντι τ. δαιμονίων, ⟦Matthew 9:34|Mt 9:34⟧; ἐν αἵματι, ⟦Hebrews 9:22|He 9:22⟧; ἐν ὕδατι, ⟦Matthew 3:11|Mt 3:11⟧, al.; ἐν μαχαίρᾳ ἀποκτενεῖ (cf. the absol. ἐν μ., ἐν ῥάβδῳ, supr., II, which some would classify here), ⟦Revelation 13:10|Re 13:10⟧ (cf. ⟦Revelation 6:8|6:8⟧). Allied to this usage and distinctly Semitic are the following: ἠγόρασας . . . ἐν τ. αἵματι σου (cf. BDB, s.v. ⁨בְּ⁩, III, 3), ⟦Revelation 5:9|Re 5:9⟧; ὁμολογεῖν ἐν (= Aram. ⁨אודי בּ⁩; cf. McNeile on Mt, I.c.; M, Pr., 104), ⟦Matthew 10:32|Mt 10:32⟧, ⟦Luke 12:8|Lk 12:8⟧; ὀμνύναι ἐν (= cl. acc., so ⟦James 5:12|Ja 5:12⟧), ⟦Matthew 5:34|Mt 5:34⟧, al.; also ⟪at the rate of, amounting to⟫, ⟦Mark 4:8|Mk 4:8⟧ (WH; vv. ll., εἰς, ἒν), ⟦Acts 7:14|Ac 7:14⟧ (LXX).
⟪IV.⟫ Of time,
	⟪(a)⟫ ⟪in⟫ or ⟪during⟫ a period: ἐν τ. ἡμέρᾳ (νυκτί), ⟦John 11:9|Jo 11:9⟧, al.; ἐν σαββάτῳ, ⟦Matthew 12:2|Mt 12:2⟧, al.; ἐν τῷ μεταξύ, ⟪meanwhile⟫, ⟦John 4:31|Jo 4:31⟧;
	⟪(b)⟫ at the time of an event: ἐν τ. παρουσίᾳ, ⟦1 Corinthians 15:23|I Co 15:23⟧; ἐν τ. ἀναστάσει, ⟦Matthew 22:28|Mt 22:28⟧;
	⟪(c)⟫ c. art. inf.,
		⟪(α)⟫ pres. (so sometimes in cl., but not as in NT = ἕως; V. M, Pr., 215), ⟪while⟫: ⟦Matthew 13:4|Mt 13:4⟧, ⟦Mark 6:48|Mk 6:48⟧, ⟦Galatians 4:18|Ga 4:18⟧, al.;
		⟪(β)⟫ aor., ⟪when, after⟫: ⟦Luke 9:36|Lk 9:36⟧, al.;
	⟪(d)⟫ ⟪within⟫ (cl.): ⟦Matthew 27:40|Mt 27:40⟧,
⟪V.⟫ In composition: (1) meaning: (a) with adjectives, it signifies usually the possession of a quality, as ἐνάλιος, ἐν́δοξος; (b) with verbs, continuance in (seq. ἐν) or motion into (seq. εἰς), as ἐμμένω, ἐμβαίνω. (ii) Assimilation: ἐν becomes ἐμ- before β, μ, π, φ, ψ; ἐγ- before γ, κ, ξ, χ; ἐλ- before λ. But in the older MSS of NT, followed by modern editions, assimilation is sometimes neglected, as in ἐνγράφω, ἐγκαινίζω, etc.

G1764.b:
⟪ἐν-ίστημι⟫
[in LXX: ⟦2 Kings 13:6|IV Ki 13:6⟧ A (⁨עמד⁩), ⟦1 Kings 12:24|III Ki 12:24⟧, I Es 5:47 9:6, ⟦Ezra 3:13|Es 3:13⟧, ⟦Ezra 3:1|1⟧; I-IV Mac 9 * ;] ⟪to place in⟫; in pf., plpf., 2 aor. and in mid., intrans.;
⟪(a)⟫ ⟪to be at hand, impend, threaten⟫: ⟦2 Timothy 3:1|II Ti 3:1⟧;
⟪(b)⟫ ⟪to be present⟫: ⟦2 Thessalonians 2:2|II Th 2:2⟧ (but v. Thayer, s.v.); pf. ptcp., ⟪present⟫: ⟦1 Corinthians 7:26|I Co 7:26⟧, ⟦Galatians 1:4|Ga 1:4⟧, ⟦Hebrews 9:9|He 9:9⟧; pl., ⟦Romans 8:38|Ro 8:38⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 3:22|I Co 3:22⟧ (Cremer, 309).†

G1709.b:
⟪ἐν-πνέω⟫, -ῶ
(Rec. ἐμπ-, v.s. ἐν) [in LXX: ⟦Deuteronomy 20:16|De 20:16⟧, ⟦Joshua 10:28|Jos 10:28⟧ ff. ⟦Joshua 11:11|Jos 11:11⟧, ⟦Joshua 11:14|14⟧ (ptcp. neut., for ⁨נֶפֶשׁ⁩, ⁨נְשָׁמָה⁩), Wi 15:11 * ;]
⟪1.⟫ ⟪to breathe on⟫.
⟪2.⟫ ⟪to breathe⟫;
⟪(a)⟫ absol.;
